IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`

§ `Chapter 2 -- General explanations`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 23, 24, 25, 26, 26B, 26C, 26D.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 23 -- Wrongful gain and wrongful loss`

-- s 23(1): a wrongful gain is gain by unlawful means of property to which the
-- person gaining it is not legally entitled, OR avoidance by unlawful means of a
-- loss of property to which the person avoiding it is not legally entitled to avoid.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 23(1)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a wrongful gain` IF
        f's `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another`
    AND f's `the intended gain is by unlawful means`
    AND (   f's `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled`
         OR f's `the intended gain is the avoidance of a loss of property which the avoider is not legally entitled to avoid`)

-- s 23(2): a wrongful loss is loss, or exposure of risk to a loss, by unlawful means
-- of property to which the person losing it or exposed to the risk of losing it is
-- legally entitled.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 23(2)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a wrongful loss` IF
        f's `intends to cause wrongful loss to another`
    AND f's `the intended loss is by unlawful means`
    AND f's `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled`

§§ `Section 24 -- Dishonestly`

-- s 24(a): intention of causing wrongful gain or wrongful loss, temporary or permanent.
-- s 24(b): dishonest by ordinary standards AND A knows that.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 24"
@export Decide whether the actor does the act dishonestly under Penal Code 1871 section 24
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements of the proposed act. Set intends to cause wrongful gain / wrongful loss and the entitlement flags for s 24(a), or both ordinary-standards flags for s 24(b).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done dishonestly` IF
        `there is a wrongful gain` f
    OR  `there is a wrongful loss` f
    OR  (    f's `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons`
         AND f's `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards`)

§§ `Section 25 -- Fraudulently`

-- Intent to deceive B and by that deception an advantage accrue or detriment befall,
-- unless so slight that no reasonable person of ordinary sense or temper would complain.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 25"
@export Decide whether the actor does the act fraudulently under Penal Code 1871 section 25
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Set intends to deceive, intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall, and whether that advantage or detriment is too slight (Explanation 1).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done fraudulently` IF
        f's `intends to deceive another person`
    AND f's `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception`
    AND NOT f's `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain`

§§ `Section 26 -- Reason to believe`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor has reason to believe` IF
    f's `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance`

§§ `Section 26B -- Good faith`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26B"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done in good faith` IF
    NOT f's `is done or believed without due care and attention`

§§ `Section 26C -- Intentionally`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26C(1)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done intentionally` IF
    f's `does the act deliberately`

§§ `Section 26D -- Knowingly`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26D(1)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done knowingly` IF
        f's `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist`
    OR  `the act is done intentionally` f
    OR  f's `is wilfully blind to the relevant circumstance`

§§ `Section 26A -- Voluntarily`

-- A person causes an effect "voluntarily" when he causes it by means whereby he
-- intended to cause it, or by means which, at the time of employing those means, he
-- knew or had reason to believe to be likely to cause it.
-- Illustration: A sets fire by night to an inhabited house to facilitate a robbery
-- and thereby causes death. A may not have intended death and may be sorry for it;
-- if he knew he was likely to cause death, he caused death voluntarily.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26A"
@export Decide whether the actor causes an effect voluntarily under Penal Code 1871 section 26A
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Either the means were those by which the actor intended to cause the effect, or, at the time of employing them, the actor knew or had reason to believe they were likely to cause it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the effect is caused voluntarily` IF
        f's `intended to cause the effect by the means employed`
    OR  f's `knew or had reason to believe the means employed were likely to cause the effect`

§§ `Section 26E -- Rashly`

-- s 26E(1): doing an act knowing there is a real risk that a particular circumstance
-- exists or will exist is doing it rashly in respect of that circumstance, if it
-- would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk.
-- s 26E(2): the same for a real risk that an effect will be caused.
-- s 26E(3): where rashness is the fault element, it is also established by
-- intention or knowledge.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26E(1) and (2)"
GIVEN f IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an unreasonable known risk was run` IF
        (   f's `knows there is a real risk that the relevant circumstance exists or will exist`
         OR f's `knows there is a real risk that the effect will be caused`)
    AND f's `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26E"
@export Decide whether the actor does the act rashly under Penal Code 1871 section 26E
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. Knowledge of a real risk (as to a circumstance or an effect) which it would have been unreasonable to take. s 26E(3): the fault element is also established where the act is done intentionally or knowingly.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done rashly` IF
        `an unreasonable known risk was run` f
    OR  `the act is done intentionally` f
    OR  `the act is done knowingly` f

§§ `Section 26F -- Negligently`

-- s 26F(1): whoever omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do, or does
-- any act which a reasonable person would not do, is said to do so negligently.
-- s 26F(2): where negligence is the fault element, it is also established where the
-- act is done intentionally, knowingly or rashly.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26F"
@export Decide whether the actor does the act negligently under Penal Code 1871 section 26F
GIVEN f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. An omission a reasonable person would not have made, or an act a reasonable person would not have done. s 26F(2): also established by intention, knowledge or rashness.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is done negligently` IF
        f's `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do`
    OR  f's `does an act which a reasonable person would not do`
    OR  `the act is done intentionally` f
    OR  `the act is done knowingly` f
    OR  `the act is done rashly` f

§§ `Section 26G -- Transferred fault`

-- s 26G(1): applies to any offence under this Code or any other written law where a
-- fault element is intention or knowledge, except where s 301(1) applies.
-- s 26G(2): where all fault and physical elements are proved and no defence applies,
-- the accused is guilty despite having believed or intended that the act or effect
-- would concern a different person or thing.
-- s 26G(3): but only where the accused did or caused those physical elements
-- negligently in respect of the person or thing actually affected.
-- s 26G(5): the accused may rely on any defence as though the act or effect had
-- concerned the person or thing he intended.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26G"
DECLARE `Transferred Fault Facts` HAS
    `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 301(1) applies to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all the fault elements and physical elements of the offence have been proven` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the physical elements included doing an act or causing an effect concerning a person or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused believed or intended the act or effect would concern a different person or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused did or caused the physical elements negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a defence or exception applies as though the act concerned the intended person or thing` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26G(1)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transferred Fault Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 26G applies to the offence` IF
        t's `a fault element of the offence is intention or knowledge`
    AND (NOT t's `section 301(1) applies to the offence`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26G(2) and (3)"
@export Decide whether transferred fault under Penal Code 1871 section 26G makes the accused guilty despite the mistake as to person or thing
GIVEN t IS A `Transferred Fault Facts` @desc The offence must have intention or knowledge as a fault element and must not be one to which s 301(1) applies. Fault transfers only where the accused was negligent in respect of the person or thing actually concerned (s 26G(3)); and s 26G(5) preserves any defence measured against the intended target.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fault is transferred under section 26G` IF
        `section 26G applies to the offence` t
    AND t's `all the fault elements and physical elements of the offence have been proven`
    AND t's `the physical elements included doing an act or causing an effect concerning a person or thing`
    AND t's `the accused believed or intended the act or effect would concern a different person or thing`
    AND t's `the accused did or caused the physical elements negligently in respect of the person or thing actually concerned`
    AND (NOT t's `a defence or exception applies as though the act concerned the intended person or thing`)

§§ `Section 26H -- Strict liability`

-- s 26H(1): an offence of strict liability is one where, for every physical element,
-- there is no corresponding fault element.
-- s 26H(2): strict liability applies to a particular physical element where there is
-- no corresponding fault element for it, whether or not the offence as a whole is
-- one of strict liability.
-- s 26H(3): an offence may be a strict liability offence though not expressly so
-- described.
-- s 26H(4): it is a defence to prove that in committing all the acts or omissions
-- that are physical elements of the offence, the accused exercised reasonable care.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26H"
DECLARE `Strict Liability Facts` HAS
    `every physical element of the offence has no corresponding fault element` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this particular physical element has no corresponding fault element` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused proves he exercised reasonable care in committing all the physical elements` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26H(1) and (3)"
GIVEN s IS A `Strict Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is one of strict liability` IF
    s's `every physical element of the offence has no corresponding fault element`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26H(2)"
GIVEN s IS A `Strict Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `strict liability applies to this physical element` IF
    s's `this particular physical element has no corresponding fault element`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 26H(4)"
@export Decide whether the reasonable-care defence to a strict liability offence under Penal Code 1871 section 26H(4) is made out
GIVEN s IS A `Strict Liability Facts` @desc The defence is available only on a charge of a strict liability offence, and requires the accused to prove reasonable care in committing all the acts or omissions that are physical elements of the offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 26H(4) reasonable care defence is made out` IF
        `the offence is one of strict liability` s
    AND s's `the accused proves he exercised reasonable care in committing all the physical elements`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Illustrations`

`s24 gain` MEANS Fault WITH
    `intends to cause wrongful gain to self or another` IS TRUE
    `intends to cause wrongful loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is of property to which the gainer is not legally entitled` IS TRUE
    `the intended gain is the avoidance of a loss of property which the avoider is not legally entitled to avoid` IS FALSE
    `the intended gain is by unlawful means` IS TRUE
    `the intended loss is of property to which the loser is legally entitled` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is an exposure to the risk of a loss` IS FALSE
    `the intended loss is by unlawful means` IS FALSE
    `the act is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `the actor knows the act is dishonest by those standards` IS FALSE
    `intends to deceive another person` IS FALSE
    `intends that an advantage accrue or a detriment befall by means of the deception` IS FALSE
    `the intended advantage or detriment is so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS FALSE
    `does the act deliberately` IS TRUE
    `has sufficient cause to believe the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is aware that the relevant circumstance exists or is virtually certain to exist` IS FALSE
    `is wilfully blind to the relevant circumstance` IS FALSE
    `is done or believed without due care and attention` IS FALSE
    `intended to cause the effect by the means employed` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe the means employed were likely to cause the effect` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the relevant circumstance exists or will exist` IS FALSE
    `knows there is a real risk that the effect will be caused` IS FALSE
    `it would have been unreasonable to have taken that risk` IS FALSE
    `omits to do an act which a reasonable person would do` IS FALSE
    `does an act which a reasonable person would not do` IS FALSE

`s24 standards` MEANS Fault WITH
